    <div class="section">
        <h2>Essential Japanese Phrases</h2>
        <div class="phrase">Hello: Konnichiwa (こんにちは)</div>
        <div class="phrase">Thank you: Arigatou gozaimasu (ありがとうございます)</div>
        <div class="phrase">Excuse me: Sumimasen (すみません)</div>
        <div class="phrase">Where is...?: ... wa doko desu ka? (〜はどこですか？)</div>
        <div class="phrase">How much?: Ikura desu ka? (いくらですか？)</div>
        <div class="phrase">I don't understand: Wakarimasen (わかりません)</div>
        <div class="phrase">Can you help me?: Tetsudatte itadakemasu ka? (手伝っていただけますか？)</div>
        <div class="phrase">Cheers!: Kanpai! (乾杯！)</div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>Travel Tips</h2>
        <div class="tip">Always carry cash, as many places don't accept credit cards.</div>
        <div class="tip">Purchase a Japan Rail Pass before arriving in Japan for cost-effective travel.</div>
        <div class="tip">Be respectful in temples and shrines; follow local customs and dress codes.</div>
        <div class="tip">Try onsen (hot springs) for a relaxing and authentic Japanese experience.</div>
        <div class="tip">Use convenience stores for quick meals, ATMs, and other services.</div>
        <div class="tip">Learn basic chopstick etiquette before your trip.</div>
        <div class="tip">Tipping is not customary in Japan; excellent service is the norm.</div>
        <div class="tip">Download offline maps and translation apps for easier navigation.</div>
    </div>
